# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository.
#
# Without this, editing on Windows rewrites a whole file to CRLF and git reports
# every line as changed: one feature branch showed 12,700 changed lines where
# ~1,400 were real, which makes a diff unreviewable. `text=auto` stores LF and
# checks out whatever the platform wants; the explicit `eol=lf` entries below
# are files that must stay LF even on Windows because something other than git
# reads them.
* text=auto

*.ts   text eol=lf
*.tsx  text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf
*.prisma text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Generated. Collapsing it in a diff keeps a lockfile bump from burying review.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff

*.png binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
